  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "New Classic God",
      "anchor": "New_Classic_God",
      "level": 2,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "title": "Chiron",
          "anchor": "Chiron",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "General",
                  "bold": true,
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Ranged Basic Attacks"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Damage Type: Physical"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Scaling Type: Strength Scaling"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Passive: Herbal Medicine",
                  "bold": true,
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Gain a charge every 12 seconds. Each time you use an ability, consume a charge to throw a poultice to an injured ally, applying a heal over time."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Healed Allies also gain Strength and Intelligence for a duration"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Poultices prioritize the ally with the lowest health in range."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Ability 1: Training Exercise",
                  "bold": true,
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Deploy a constellation, granting Crowd Control immunity to  teammates in the area. After a 1 second delay, it explodes dealing Physical Damage to all enemies in the area."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Ability 2: Masterful Shot",
                  "bold": true,
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Chiron applies Target Mark when he damages enemies with abilities, reducing their physical protections by 10%. Activating this ability fires a seeking arrows toward all marked targets, dealing Physical Damage and slowing them."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Once Chiron has 250 Strength he is able to fire a second larger arrow in a targeted area, dealing 100% of initial damage, plus 15% bonus damage per hit by masterful shot, up to 4 targets."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Once Chiron has 2.5 attack speed, Masterful Shot becomes Masterful Flurry. Firing 3 arrows with lower scaling quickly at each target, which proc basic attack item effects."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Ability 3: Giddyup!",
                  "bold": true,
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Gallop forward dealing Physical Damage to enemies, knocking up minions, and kicking enemy gods behind you."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Chiron is displacement immune while charging"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Chiron may fire basic attacks and Masterful Shot while charging."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Ultimate Ability: Centaurus",
                  "bold": true,
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Transform into a constellation, lowering movement speed but gaining the ability to fire three long distance arrows that pass through walls dealing Physical Damage to all enemies they hit."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "If Chiron would be killed during this ability, he does not die until he runs out of time or shots."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "If Chiron would have died, but killed an enemy with his ability, he is returned to life with health equal to the damage dealt instead."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Chiron can fire Masterful Shot during this ability"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Aspect of the Heroic Tutor releasing Jan. 30",
                  "bold": true,
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Chiron’s Target Mark now only applies to one target and he passively copies 10% of damage done to that target, dealing it again as physical damage."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Training Exercise boosts allies Strength and Intelligence when it applies to CC immunity and again when it bursts."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Centaurus has less damage scaling, but slows enemies and grants allies it hits an attack speed buff as well as a shield and .5 seconds of CC immunity."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "New Event and Saga: Reign Of the Archfiend",
      "anchor": "New_Event_and_Saga:_Reign_Of_the_Archfiend",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Reign of the Archfiend is a new kind of event for SMITE 2, inspired by the fan-favorite Buy All events in SMITE 1 – kind of like a Season Pass."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "For one heavily discounted purchase price, you can unlock all new Wandering Market cosmetic content that will be released in SMITE 2 through the end of March. This includes:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "One Legendary Saga: The Archfiend Saga Kukulkan"
            },
            {
              "text": "Two Reward Travelers",
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Ra’nhur Best Friends"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Reward Traveler for Mordred"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Classic Travelers for Eight Gods",
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Da Ji, Discordia, Neith, Janus, Loki, Sol, Artio, and Tsukuyomi"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Premium Travelers for Two Gods",
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Dragonheart Rebel Jing Wei, Artemis"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "An Additional Collection of Reward Cosmetics",
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Two Titles, a Card Effect, a Ward"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "All of this content can be unlocked for the discounted price of 8,000 Diamonds."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "If you just want to buy a few new Travelers during the event, don’t worry: Travelers will still be available at their normal prices."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "If you are buying Travelers outside of the buy-all, you will accumulate Wyrm Seals with each Traveler purchased and unlock rewards gradually. Two Wyrm Seals are available completely for free on the Wandering Market Path, which is refreshing with this update. You will unlock rewards based on the number of Wyrm Seals you collect before the event’s end – including The Archfiend Saga itself."
        }
      ],
